      "date": "2026-08-06 05:23:15.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(3 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nMechanically this is clean dead-code removal and nothing in the tree still references any of the eight helpers. One whole-patch thought though: all four of these headers are installed into $(includedir)/linux/lustre by the install-data-local rule in autoMakefile.am, so they are the shipped client API and not just internal kernel headers. \"Never called\" was necessarily verified only inside lustre-release; two of the removed inlines are the consumer-side half of accessor pairs whose producer-side half stays, so they look unused for a structural reason rather than because nobody wants them. Comments inline.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    },
